ons":["f51891e0-595e-4989-b831-332f02aa38b7"],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":"02964b80a45012bfb16762d700160376ec0412de","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Landed at 02964b80 (worker fea446d8 + foreman follow-up 02964b80). mcp status now probes the state DB through the CLI's stateDatabaseProblem() helper and exits 1 with the CorruptStateDatabaseError wording on a corrupt file (measured: 4KB random bytes -> exit 1 + diagnostic + recovery pointer; absent DB -> unchanged exit 0 'Not running'). The stale compiled specs/ralph-loop.spec.dir/src/controller.js (bare new Database) is gone, along with its orphaned compiled index, and tests/db/compiled-artifact-guard.test.ts pins that no tracked specs/**/src/*.js constructs the DB outside the guarded opener. Red-proof: 3 of 9 new tests FAIL at base ef9b12b9, 9/9 PASS after. Gates on merged tree: build 0, tsc --noEmit 0, lint 0 errors, full suite 115 files passed | 4 skipped, 1958 tests passed | 0 failed; CI on 02964b80 = success. Tier-2 run c62e9f0a: tier1 PASS, tier2 INCOMPLETE/CAP (0 of 1 criteria graded; the single criterion was compound and the judge hit its 100-iteration cap at 631,868 input tokens \u2014 no substantive judgement made). Row closed on foreman-verified gates + green CI with that caveat; QA-SPECLANG-010 carries the layer-level residual.","depends_on":[]}
-{"id":"CFG-SPECLANG-1","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"chore","complexity":2,"title":"Fleet config: two enabled foreman rows for this one repo spawn in pairs and collide (owner decision needed)","reasoning":"scheduler.db projects carries BOTH 'SpecLang-foreman' (workdir /home/kara/SpecLang) and 'speclang-foreman' (workdir /home/kara/speclang), each enabled=1, admission_mode=tasks, cooldown_s=21600. They therefore spawn in pairs at the same spawned_at: on 2026-11-17 the spawns 05-00-08, 06-20-29 and 07-42-14 EACH appear twice in the ticks table, once per row. Observed cost: two foremen ran concurrently in two checkouts of the same repo; the second had to stand down from the first's rows, and both could collide on board commits and merges to origin/main.","acceptance_criteria":"OWNER-GATED - no worker may edit scheduler config. Owner picks one of: (a) disable one of the two project rows (PUT /api/v1/projects/<name> enabled=false, then regenerate the fleet.toml mirror with fleet-sync.py --write), or (b) keep both but give them disjoint ownership (separate boards / lane scopes) and document which rows each owns. Proof after the change: over the next 3 scheduled cycles scheduler.db ticks shows exactly ONE running foreman row per spawn time for this repo (today every spawn time has two) and the fleet.toml mirror carries exactly one enabled foreman lane for SpecLang.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"ed1fabc06322224e50a524fc8f5e82f08bd4dc037ccb9e7b4243bf2873a9c32d"},"capability_tags":[],"created_at":"2026-11-17T09:26:16.712417+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T09:26:16.712417+00:00","foreman_note":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"depends_on":[],"deferred":true,"defer_reason":"needs an owner decision: which of the two foreman rows is authoritative","defer_review_by":"2026-11-24"}
