 {"id":"UX-004-R1","status":"pending","priority":"P4","type":"bug","complexity":3,"title":"P4 — SUPPORT.md:15 advertises GitHub Discussions, which is not enabled on the repo (dead support channel)","reasoning":"Found by the gitreins tier-2 judge for UX-004 (verdict 1d25bff7) and re-verified by the foreman at HEAD on 2026-11-17:\n  SUPPORT.md:15  - **Discussions:** [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/dexdat/SpecLang/discussions)\n  gh api repos/dexdat/SpecLang --jq '{has_discussions, has_issues}' -> {\"archived\":false,\"has_discussions\":false,\"has_issues\":true}\n  The same tick's new .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml:5-8 states in a comment that GitHub Discussions is NOT enabled, so the tree now contradicts itself: the issue-template chooser routes users to the issue tracker while SUPPORT.md still sends them to a Discussions page that does not exist for this repo. A stranger following SUPPORT.md reaches a dead channel.\n  Doc-severity P4 per the doc-lane ruling (policy cap, not a new assessment of the finding).\n  FIX: either remove the Discussions bullet from SUPPORT.md and name the issue tracker as the single support channel (matching config.yml), or enable Discussions and link it. Do not invent a third channel.","acceptance_criteria":"From the repo root: (1) SUPPORT.md no longer lists a Discussions channel that does not exist — `grep -ci discussions SUPPORT.md` prints 0, OR the bullet is replaced by a link to a channel that is actually enabled and `gh api repos/dexdat/SpecLang --jq .has_discussions` prints true when the bullet is kept; (2) whichever state is chosen, .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml and SUPPORT.md agree — the channel named in one is named in the other and no file claims Discussions is disabled while another advertises it (`grep -rn -i discussions SUPPORT.md .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml` read side by side); (3) the remaining support links resolve (gh api for the repo's has_issues=true). Evidence: the greps and the gh api output pasted.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"5c89716b942b6020ec1c4ba1837559f32700b6d8b43cc472f13f97d02bde3938"},"capability_tags":["docs","support"],"created_at":"2026-11-17T10:45:25.457739+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T10:45:25.457739+00:00","foreman_note":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"depends_on":[]}
 {"id":"QA-SPECLANG-010","status":"pending","priority":"P3","type":"bug","complexity":3,"title":"P3 — the tracked compiled spec-dir layer is systematically stale: 29 dangling relative requires, and specs/sqlite.spec.dir/src/index.js predates the corruption guard its .ts carries","reasoning":"Found while reviewing QA-SPECLANG-5-R6 (2026-11-17). A static scan of every tracked specs/**/src/*.js (576 relative requires at base ef9b12b9) reports 29 that resolve to nothing, e.g. '../utils.js' (8 files), '../../../mcp.spec.dir/src/server.js' (2), '../../../parser.spec.dir/src/validator.js'. Separately, specs/sqlite.spec.dir/src/index.js carries none of the CorruptStateDatabaseError/openStateDatabase surface that specs/sqlite.spec.dir/src/index.ts:39 defines, so a consumer loading the compiled copy bypasses the guard that the TS source installs. tests/workflow/conversation.test.ts already imports a spec-dir .js copy at runtime ('Runtime under test: specs/workflow.spec.dir/src/conversation.js'), so this layer is not inert.","acceptance_criteria":"(1) A scripted audit exists and runs in CI: for every tracked specs/**/src/*.js, resolve each relative require('./x'|'../x') against the tree and fail on unresolved targets, with the current 29 baseline either fixed or explicitly listed as accepted-and-why. (2) A decision is recorded and enforced for the compiled spec-dir layer: regenerate it from the .ts sources or retire it — no third state where a tracked .js silently differs from its .ts in a guard-bearing module. Proof for (2): for every spec-dir module whose .ts exports a state-DB opener or corruption diagnostic, the tracked .js exports the same symbol set (test asserts the symbol lists match). (3) npm run build, npm run lint and the full suite stay green.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"d8563d05c24732eb1f9f4d68d5aaddd4511f345a5da997b2e65be1993e2cfc91"},"capability_tags":[],"created_at":"2026-11-17T10:57:30.456892+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T10:57:30.456892+00:00","